\section{Cross-Architecture Comparison}
\label{app:cross_arch}

Table~\ref{tab:cross_arch} evaluates on Mistral-7B-v0.3~\cite{jiang2023mistral} (GQA + sliding window, dense PPL 5.52).

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Cross-architecture comparison (WikiText-2 PPL$\downarrow$). Adv = TEAL\,/\,KL ratio. LLaMA uses global top-$k$; Mistral uses uniform allocation (matched within each architecture).}
\label{tab:cross_arch}
\small
\begin{tabular}{l@{\hspace{4pt}}cc@{\hspace{3pt}}c@{\hspace{6pt}}|@{\hspace{6pt}}cc@{\hspace{3pt}}c}
\toprule
 & \multicolumn{3}{c}{Mistral-7B} & \multicolumn{3}{c}{LLaMA-8B} \\
 & KL & TEAL & Adv & KL & TEAL & Adv \\
\midrule
30\% & \textbf{6.77} & 8.38 & 1.24$\times$ & \textbf{8.96} & 10.97 & 1.22$\times$ \\ % exp_id: kl_30_mistral, teal_30_mistral, kl30_3seed_global
50\% & \textbf{8.65} & 18.31 & 2.12$\times$ & \textbf{11.79} & 23.31 & 1.98$\times$ \\ % exp_id: kl_50_mistral, teal_50_mistral
70\% & \textbf{13.33} & 61.72 & 4.63$\times$ & \textbf{17.91} & 100.11 & 5.59$\times$ \\ % exp_id: kl_70_mistral, teal_70_mistral
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

The KL PPL advantage ratio is consistent across architectures (within 8\% at $\leq$50\% sparsity).
Table~\ref{tab:mistral_downstream} reports downstream task accuracy at 30\% sparsity on Mistral-7B-v0.3, confirming that KL's downstream advantage generalizes across architectures.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Mistral-7B-v0.3 downstream evaluation at 30\% sparsity (seed 42). KL outperforms TEAL on 5 of 6 tasks (largest: ARC-c +9.0pp, HellaSwag +8.8pp); GSM8K is the sole reversal.}
\label{tab:mistral_downstream}
\small
\resizebox{\columnwidth}{!}{
\begin{tabular}{lccccccc}
\toprule
Method & PPL$\downarrow$ & ARC-c & WG & HS & PIQA & MMLU & GSM8K \\
\midrule
Dense & 5.06 & 54.4 & 73.2 & 77.9 & 80.1 & 62.5 & 37.8 \\
KL 30\% & \textbf{6.77} & \textbf{50.2} & \textbf{69.1} & \textbf{68.9} & \textbf{75.2} & \textbf{44.0} & 11.1 \\ % exp_id: mistral_kl30_downstream
TEAL 30\% & 8.38 & 41.1 & 63.5 & 60.1 & 72.1 & 43.5 & \textbf{15.9} \\ % exp_id: mistral_teal30_downstream
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}}
\end{table}


\section{SPON Orthogonality}
\label{app:spon}

SPON~\cite{xu2026spon} bias correction is weakly correlated with the KL predictor (cosine similarity 0.196, $R^2$=0.038) and yields only 2.4\% PPL improvement (12.08$\to$11.79); the predictor already captures most recoverable signal. % exp_id: spon_decomposition, spon_2048_s42, mvp_kl_norm_v2_s42
The decomposition confirms that SPON and the KL predictor operate on largely orthogonal error sources.

